   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = - 2 x^{2} + 15 x - 26 \\) and \\( g(x) = - x - 2 \\). The shaded region R shown is bounded by the graphs of f and g. Find the exact area of R.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         64,
         3
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Setting \\( f(x) = g(x) \\) gives \\( - 2 x^{2} + 16 x - 24 = 0 \\), so the curves meet at \\( x = 2 \\) and \\( x = 6 \\), and f is above g between them.",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99059",
         "rule_named": "upper minus lower"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The area is \\( \\int_{2}^{6} \\left(- 2 x^{2} + 16 x - 24\\right)\\,dx \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99001",
         "rule_named": "area between curves"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "An antiderivative of the integrand is \\( - \\frac{2 x^{3}}{3} + 8 x^{2} - 24 x \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99003",
         "rule_named": "power rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluating from \\( 2 \\) to \\( 6 \\), the area is \\( \\frac{64}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            64,
            3
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
         "rule_named": "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus"
      }
   ],
   "options": [
